From michael.watson at bbsrc.ac.uk  Fri May 27 17:43:22 2005
From: michael.watson at bbsrc.ac.uk (michael watson (IAH-C))
Date: Fri May 27 17:43:59 2005
Subject: [BioC] limma reading wrong column for GPR files
Message-ID: <8975119BCD0AC5419D61A9CF1A923E950121BC03@iahce2knas1.iah.bbsrc.reserved>

As far as I know this is correct for limma - the default is to read the mean of pixels for foreground and the median of pixels for background.  The reason being that the median is less sensitive to outliers, and you are more likely to get those in the background.

You can always use the "columns" argument of read.maimages to change this eg:

RG <- read.maimages(blah, blah, blah, columns = list(Rf = "F635 Mean", Rb = "B635 Mean", Gf = "F532 Mean", Gb = "B532 Mean"))

Mick


